<article class="env-proposition" id="11051A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/11051A">Proposition <span data-tag="11051A">5.2.5.1</span>.</a> Suppose given an adjunction of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix {\calC  \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{F} &amp;  \calD  \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{G}}. \]
</div>
  <p> Assume that the $\infty $-category $\calC $ admits pullbacks, and let $C$ be an object of $\calC $. Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The induced functor $f: \calC ^{/C} \rightarrow \calD ^{/FC}$ admits a right adjoint $g$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The functor $g$ is equivalent to the composition 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \calD ^{/FC} \stackrel{g'}{\rightarrow } \calC ^{/GFC} \stackrel{g''}{\rightarrow } \calC ^{/C}, \]
</div>
<p>
 where $g'$ is induced by $G$ and $g''$ is induced by pullback along the unit map $C \rightarrow GFC$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>